Relevant columns and how they will be used  

variants.reference_name : chromosome filter ( = 'X')  
variants.start : genomic coordinate – used to exclude two pseudo‑autosomal regions  
variants.reference_bases : reference allele; together with alternate_bases lets us keep only SNPs (length = 1)  
variants.alternate_bases : list of alternate alleles; keep only records where exactly one single‑base alt is present  
variants.call : repeated STRUCT that contains per‑sample genotype information  
 • call.call_set_name : sample / individual ID – used for grouping  
 • call.genotype : ARRAY<INT64> – the alleles we classify  
 • (any other fields in call are not needed here)  

Conditions that will be applied  

reference_name = 'X'  
NOT (start BETWEEN 59999 AND 2699519 OR start BETWEEN 154931042 AND 155260559)  
LENGTH(reference_bases)=1  
ARRAY_LENGTH(alternate_bases)=1 AND LENGTH(alternate_bases[OFFSET(0)])=1  
ARRAY_LENGTH(call.genotype) > 0  

